// Title: Startup Folder File Write
// Sigma ID: 2aa0a6b4-a865-495b-ab51-c28249537b75
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Roberto Rodriguez (Cyb3rWard0g), OTR (Open Threat Research)
// Date: 2020-05-02 | Modified: 2025-12-03
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.001
// Description: A General detection for files being created in the Windows startup directory. This could be an
//   indicator of persistence.
// False positives:
//   - FP could be caused by legitimate application writing shortcuts for example. This folder should always be inspected to make sure that all the files in there are legitimate
// References:
//   - https://github.com/OTRF/detection-hackathon-apt29/issues/12
//   - https://github.com/OTRF/ThreatHunter-Playbook/blob/2d4257f630f4c9770f78d0c1df059f891ffc3fec/docs/evals/apt29/detections/5.B.1_611FCA99-97D0-4873-9E51-1C1BA2DBB40D.md
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_startup_folder_file_write.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Start Menu\\Programs\\StartUp" and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath in~ ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\wuauclt.exe", "C:\\Windows\\uus\\ARM64\\wuaucltcore.exe")) or (FolderPath startswith "C:\\$WINDOWS.~BT\\NewOS\\" or FolderPath startswith "C:\\$WinREAgent\\Scratch\\Mount\\")))) and (not((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\ONENOTE.EXE" and FolderPath endswith "\\Send to OneNote.lnk")))
